Here's a simple Java program that prompts the user to enter two positive integers and then computes and displays their Greatest Common Divisor (GCD):

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class GCDCalculator {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);

        int num1 = 0, num2 = 0;

        // Prompt user for the first positive integer
        do {
            System.out.print("Enter the first positive integer: ");
            if (scanner.hasNextInt()) {
                num1 = scanner.nextInt();
                if (num1 <= 0) {
                    System.out.println("Please enter a positive integer.");
                }
            } else {
                System.out.println("Invalid input. Please enter a positive integer.");
                scanner.next(); // discard invalid input
            }
        } while (num1 <= 0);

        // Prompt user for the second positive integer
        do {
            System.out.print("Enter the second positive integer: ");
            if (scanner.hasNextInt()) {
                num2 = scanner.nextInt();
                if (num2 <= 0) {
                    System.out.println("Please enter a positive integer.");
                }
            } else {
                System.out.println("Invalid input. Please enter a positive integer.");
                scanner.next(); // discard invalid input
            }
        } while (num2 <= 0);

        int gcd = computeGCD(num1, num2);

        System.out.println("The GCD of " + num1 + " and " + num2 + " is: " + gcd);

        scanner.close();
    }

    // Method to compute GCD using Euclidean algorithm
    public static int computeGCD(int a, int b) {
        while (b != 0) {
            int temp = b;
            b = a % b;
            a = temp;
        }
        return a;
    }
}
```

**How it works:**

- The program prompts the user to enter two positive integers, validating the input.
- It uses the Euclidean algorithm to compute the GCD efficiently.
- Finally, it displays the result.

